{"qid":"Q881","names":["Socialist Republic of Vietnam"],"title":"Socialist Republic of Vietnam","endonym":{"native":"Việt Nam","lang":"vi"},"capsule":"The Socialist Republic of Vietnam was proclaimed on 2 July 1976 following the reunification of North and South Vietnam after the fall of Saigon on 30 April 1975, with Hanoi as capital and the Vietnamese Communist Party as the single ruling authority under General Secretary Le Duan until his death in 1986. The Doi Moi economic reforms adopted at the Sixth Party Congress in December 1986 dismantled central planning in favor of a socialist-oriented market economy, producing sustained GDP growth averaging 6–8% annually through the 1990s and 2000s and lifting tens of millions out of poverty. Vietnam joined ASEAN in 1995, normalized relations with the United States the same year, and acceded to the WTO in 2007, integrating into global trade as a major manufacturing hub. The state remains governed by the Communist Party and continues to exist as of the dataset's attestation end.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Vietnam's contemporary boundaries and political history are fully documented; the attestation end of 2025 reflects the dataset's present-day horizon.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Vietnam","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam"},{"label":"Britannica: Vietnam","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Vietnam"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Doi Moi","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_Moi"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Reunification of Vietnam","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reunification_of_Vietnam"}],"britannica":"place/Vietnam","cowCode"